## CQ-RPS-15 | Food Dictionary Hardest sort; Diet Log width default 48 (#27, #28)
@group client
@commands Client with `rps only`, fresh `config/` (jar defaults). Open the Diet Log; read `config/solraspberrypie-client.toml`; set `[foodDictionary] uneatenSort = "HARDEST"`, reopen the Food Dictionary uneaten pages; set `"EASIEST"`, reopen (RPS-15)
@pass the generated config has `extraWidth = 48` and lists `HARDEST` after `EASIEST` in the uneatenSort comment and allowed values; Hardest lists the uneaten foods from the highest base diversity down (ties: more hunger first), Easiest the reverse order of base diversity; the Diet Log opens at the same about 25% extra width as before
@fails `RpConfig.UneatenSort`, `client/FoodDictionarySort.uneaten`; `RpConfig` `extraWidth`
@reviewed 2026-11-24
@modset rps only +"creativecommon-*" +"creativedevtools-*" +"kubejs-forge-*" +"rhino-forge-*" +"architectury-*"
# steps written r1124gate 2026-11-24 (runner-4): pair run with `--config config/solraspberrypie-client.toml:dietLog:extraWidth='"x"'` (a string for an int key; -1 was clamped to 0, not the default)
# on the client (section 1 text): Forge corrects the out-of-range value to the jar default and rewrites the file with the
# jar's comments, which stands in for a fresh config (serve copies the pack's config/). Sort changes go through Forge's
# own config watcher (Raspberry Pie is stamped) while the game runs; each edit waits for its reload line (lint W cfgedit).
cli:bootexpect dietLog\.extraWidth.*corrected from .*x.* to its default, 48
srv> op @a
srv> gamemode survival @a
srv> difficulty easy
srv> time set noon
srv> solrp reset @a
srv> clear @a
srv> effect clear @a
sleep 2
cli:shell grep -nE "extraWidth|HARDEST|EASIEST|uneatenSort =" config/solraspberrypie-client.toml
cli:shell grep -q "^[[:space:]]*extraWidth = 48" config/solraspberrypie-client.toml
cli:shell grep -E "Allowed Values: .*EASIEST, HARDEST" config/solraspberrypie-client.toml
srv> item replace entity @a hotbar.0 with solapplepie:food_book
sleep 1
do {"slot": 0}
do {"use": "item"}
do {"wait": "screen:FoodBookScreen"}
shot diet_log_width
do {"screen": "close"}
cli:shell python3 "$INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py" toml config/solraspberrypie-client.toml foodDictionary uneatenSort '"HARDEST"'
cli:waitlog \[creativecommon\] solraspberrypie-client\.toml reloaded 20
srv> item replace entity @a hotbar.0 with solcarrot:food_book
sleep 1
do {"slot": 0}
do {"use": "item"}
do {"wait": "screen:FoodBookScreen"}
