## CQ-RPS-12 | isolated client: Diet Log from any food; a dedicated server's table reaches the client (PR-RP-12, PR-RP-17)
@group client
@commands Dedicated server with `rps only` whose Raspberry Pie copy carries an extra table (`rps_fixture.py table "mods/solRaspberryPie-*.jar" rps12 '{"values": {"minecraft:bread": 7.25}}'`); the client runs the plain jar (no such table). Join; hover bread; craft book + rotten flesh, book + cooked cod, book + golden carrot, book + carrot, book + potion; open the Liquid Diet Log after drinking two potions, eat a food, drink a third (RPS-12)
@pass client log: one `Diversity table from the server: 1 values, 0 family members; 0 ids unknown to this client`; bread's tooltip diversity value is 7.25 (the server's), not Apple Pie's own; book + rotten flesh, cooked cod and golden carrot each give a Diet Log; book + carrot stays the Food Dictionary's recipe and book + potion gives the Liquid Diet Log; the Liquid Diet Log lists the drinks newest first, still after the food (the state sync without a drink list keeps the client's list) and with the third drink on top
@fails `net/S2CDiversity.java`, `logic/Diversity.java` (`load` must not read the client's jars without an integrated server; `applyRemote`), `ServerEvents.datapackSync`; `recipe/EdibleIngredient.java`; `S2CState.hasDrinks` and `ClientState.setState` (drink list kept)
@reviewed 2026-11-24
# steps written r1124gate 2026-11-24 (runner-4): pair run; the server copy of the Raspberry Pie jar carries rps12.json
# (section @@prep, by hand for a pair run: `qrun.py prep`), the client the plain jar
cli:bootexpect Diversity table from the server: 1 values, 0 family members; 0 ids unknown to this client
cli:shell grep -c "Diversity table from the server" logs/latest.log; test "$(grep -c "Diversity table from the server" logs/latest.log)" = 1
